      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine for adults is 10 mg. Usual doses are 2.5 to 10 mg once daily. 50 mg is five times the maximum and could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed clinician with prescribing authority. I can't confirm that this order was actually requested for the patient.\n\nI can enter the order once a prescriber confirms the intended dose, or if the prescriber is the one asking me to enter it. For example, if the intended order is amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily, they can tell me and I'll enter it."
      }
